# Obsidian safety

## Read-only default

List/search notes and create/edit a named note are fine when Obsidian work is
authorized. Do **not**:

- delete notes or folders
- move or rename notes (breaks wikilinks unless updated)
- bulk-rewrite or mass-retag across folders the user did not name
- wipe or rewrite `.obsidian/` app config
- empty the vault trash / permanently purge

…unless the user gave an explicit verb this turn naming the object(s).

When renaming or moving with authorization, update inbound `[[wikilinks]]` in
the same change when cheap to find; say what was left unresolved.

Never paste credentials, tokens, or full private journal dumps into chat.
Summarize; cite paths.
